# Directory Structure — Vue 3

```
src/
├── main.ts                     ← Bootstrap app
├── App.vue                     ← Root component
├── router/
│   └── index.ts                ← Vue Router config
├── stores/                     ← Pinia stores (one file per domain)
│   └── useUserStore.ts
├── composables/                ← Reusable composition functions
│   └── useAuth.ts
├── components/
│   ├── atoms/                  ← Smallest units, no internal state (AppButton, AppInput)
│   ├── molecules/              ← Composed from atoms (FormField, SearchBar)
│   └── organisms/              ← Complex components (AppHeader, DataTable)
├── views/                      ← Page-level components (1-to-1 with routes)
│   └── HomeView.vue
├── types/
│   └── index.ts                ← Shared TypeScript types
└── utils/
    └── index.ts                ← Pure utility functions
```

## Principles

- **`views/`** are shells only — orchestrate composables and organisms, no complex logic
- **`composables/`** for reusable logic — naming: `use<Domain>.ts`
- **`stores/`** only for global state — keep local state inside the component
- **Component files** use PascalCase: `AppButton.vue`, `UserCard.vue`
